            <ArticleTitle>Hemivertebra of the cervical spine: an uncommon background for neck pain, cervical scoliosis, and torticollis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1718-1719</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1144</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 15-year-old female patient presented with neck pain accompanied by cervical scoliosis, on the existence of torticollis. Although rare, hemivertebra of the cervical spine is a congenital deformation associated with these three clinical features.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
